From 8c74a55f7113046152ea6667404eb45f08794b23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rautshivamxyz-beep <rautshivamxyz@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:40:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v9.33.151 "An append is not a save"

v9.33.90 gave NOVA one way to save a file: NcieFiles.write, which writes a
sibling .tmp and renames it over the target, takes one lock per destination
path, and answers false instead of throwing. v9.33.131 then routed the skill
forge's append through NcieFiles.append for the same three reasons. Ten bare
File.appendText calls were still outside that.

An appendText is a buffered stream straight onto the file. It takes no lock,
so the tutor's background write and a foreground one can interleave their
bytes into one torn line. It is not atomic, so a kill mid-append leaves half
a line where a whole one was expected. And it appends happily to a file NOVA
could not read - writing a second half onto a damaged whole, which is the one
thing NcieFiles.append exists to refuse.

The eight that write small state files are gone: the tutor's missed questions
and missed flashcards, its new flashcards, the growth ledger's turn and skill
lines, the trigger store, and a remembered place. Two stay, and now say why
in the code: the notification and auto-reply logs are logs (losing a line
costs nothing, and reading a 512 KB log back per notification to rewrite it
would cost a lot), and the wiki store is several megabytes indexed by byte
offset - rewriting it per article would copy the whole store and invalidate
every offset.

The same doctrine has a second half, and these six sites dropped it with no
catch at all: a save whose ANSWER is discarded cannot fail visibly either.
v9.33.147 fixed the call sites that wrapped a write in a catch; these dropped
the boolean outright. The learned snapshot, the value counts that decide
which sources earn their place in the prompt, the grounding index, the
trigger delete and the recipe output all hear their save now - and the two
places that then spoke to the user follow it: a flashcard is only announced
as saved when it was saved, a recipe file is not "Wrote x.txt" over nothing
on disk, and the voice language is not announced as changed when the file
did not take it.

Also, and only because it is now a read-modify-write: the trigger store's
removeAt refuses a list it could not read (the v9.33.119 rule) instead of
rewriting every trigger the user had out of an empty list.

The checks hold the sweep: no bare appendText survives in the six swept
files, the two deliberate exceptions still use it and still say why, every
converted site goes through the one save, and each save that now has an
answer reports it.
